:name: @NAME@ (Linux on a Cortex-A9 Zynq model)
:description: Boots $vmlinux + $dtb + $rootfs (initrd); defaults: the cached Zynq-7000 buildroot demo of renode-box.
# Your Yocto/buildroot images: set $vmlinux, $dtb, $rootfs before `include`. $demos is set by the .robot
# (or: ./renode-box renode -e '$demos=@<renode-box>/cache/downloads; include @@NAME@.resc; start').
$vmlinux?=$demos/zynq-interface-tests-vmlinux-s_14142952-ab5cd7445f31414fcbf8c79d49d737c669034ef2
$rootfs?=$demos/zynq--interface-tests-rootfs.ext2-s_16777216-191638e3b3832a81bebd21d555f67bf3a4d7882a
$dtb?=$demos/zynq-interface-tests-gem0.dtb-s_11724-f0dec8ffadea47891dfe2441215401f09f7242fa
$bootargs?="console=ttyPS0,115200 root=/dev/ram0 rw initrd=0x1a000000,16M"

using sysbus
mach create "@NAME@"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/zedboard.repl
showAnalyzer uart0
sysbus Redirect 0xC0000000 0x0 0x10000000
ttc0 Frequency 33333333
ttc1 Frequency 33333333

macro reset
"""
    cpu SetRegister 0 0x000
    cpu SetRegister 1 0xD32
    cpu SetRegister 2 0x100
    sysbus LoadELF $vmlinux
    sysbus LoadFdt $dtb 0x100 $bootargs false
    sysbus ZeroRange 0x1a000000 0x1600000
    sysbus LoadBinary $rootfs 0x1a000000
"""
runMacro $reset
